# Repositories

## File layout

- `index.go` — `{Domain}Repo` interface + `New{Domain}Repo(dbdget db.DBGormDelegate)`
- `repo.go` — GORM queries
- `struct.go` — join DTOs (optional)

## Pattern (matches user/repo.go)

```go
type userRepo struct {
    dbdget db.DBGormDelegate
}

func (r *userRepo) GetByID(ctx context.Context, id uint) (*model.User, error) {
    user := &model.User{}
    q := r.dbdget.Get(ctx).Where("id = ?", id).First(user)
    if q.Error != nil {
        if q.Error == gorm.ErrRecordNotFound {
            return nil, errors.From("DATA_NOT_FOUND")
        }
        return nil, q.Error
    }
    return user, nil
}

func (r *userRepo) Update(ctx context.Context, m model.User, updatedFields ...string) (int64, error) {
    if len(updatedFields) == 0 {
        return 0, errors.From("BAD_REQUEST")
    }
    updatedFields = append(updatedFields, "updated_at")
    query := r.dbdget.Get(ctx).Model(&m).Where("id = ?", m.ID).Select(updatedFields).Updates(m)
    return query.RowsAffected, query.Error
}
```

## Rules

- Always `r.dbdget.Get(ctx)` (respects tx from `txRepo.Run`)
- Map not-found in repo, not service
- No business logic; only own service may call this repo
